      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Focusing on systemic injustices and how power has been used is the only way to truly prepare students for the real world and foster critical thinking. Teaching only about \"wins\" and shared values creates a distorted history that ignores the struggles of marginalized groups and fails to equip students with the tools to challenge inequality. Middle schoolers need to understand the full, complex picture of our nation's past, including its failures, to build a more just and informed future.",
